---
title: "Secrets"
---

This project uses the `sops-age` advisory profile for encrypted committed secret/config files.

## Principles

- Keep private age keys outside the repository.
- Commit encrypted `*.sops.*` files only when encrypted repository storage is intentional.
- Do not commit decrypted plaintext, `.env`, API keys, tokens, private keys, or credential JSON.
- Prefer `sops exec-env` when possible so plaintext is injected into the process instead of written to disk.

## Common Commands

Run a command with encrypted dotenv values:

```bash
sops exec-env secrets/local.sops.env 'uv run <command>'
```

Temporarily decrypt for tools that require `.env`:

```bash
sops -d secrets/local.sops.env > .env
```

Edit encrypted values:

```bash
sops secrets/local.sops.env
```

